From 3fae561d2b67908f99ab7c5ccb8a798f86a46b82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iwanicki92 <iwanicki92@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:59:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Print to the framebuffer GRUB describes in the SLRT

With DEBUG, print() also draws on a linear framebuffer when GRUB adds
its debug-only SLRT entry for one, so the SKL's progress shows on a
platform without a serial port. Output starts at the line GRUB stopped
at. Hex dumps go to the serial port only, they would scroll everything
else off the screen.

The address comes from unmeasured bootloader data, so a framebuffer that
overlaps the SLB, or reaches above 4 GiB where neither build can address
it, is refused. The glyphs are the ASCII part of the X11 misc-fixed 8x16
font, which is public domain.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [debug]
Signed-off-by: iwanicki92 <iwanicki92@gmail.com>
---
 fb.c             | 363 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/printk.h |   3 +
 include/slrt.h   |  17 +++
 main.c           |   4 +
 printk.c         |  12 ++
 5 files changed, 399 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 fb.c

diff --git a/fb.c b/fb.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..99378eb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/fb.c
@@ -0,0 +1,363 @@
